<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="d5520f41">&lt;p&gt;
    If the program requires large-scale classroom training, consider reserving rooms in the necessary locations. Most
    clients have dedicated but limited learning spaces. Therefore, it&apos;s crucial to establish a good relationship with the
    internal teams who manage these spaces, as their support will be needed in terms of managing room bookings and
    audio-visual requirements.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Consider external locations as a possible alternative if internal space is limited.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Clearly identify and communicate who is responsible for managing all learning logistics. Inform this team about any
    changes and confirm they have sufficient resources and capacity to provide support.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
